      "content": "One common pitfall is the failure to disclose assets in offshore trusts, shell companies, or complex structures. HMRC may use various methods to identify these assets, including information exchange agreements with foreign tax authorities, anti-money laundering databases, and subsidiaries' tax returns. However, they rely heavily on voluntary disclosures and cooperation from estates to identify and report these assets. Those assets not disclosed in initial probate filings, such as those held in complex structures or newly discovered assets, may be subject to penalties and increased tax liabilities if not volunteered.",
